"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:1107-06-01:0":{"b": ["Surkhab b. Badr dies (Shawwal 500 / June 1107); Abu Mansur succeeds him.", "a1931e53"], "d": ["Surkhab b. Badr dies (Shawwal 500 / June 1107); Abu Mansur succeeds him.", "a1931e53"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:1109-07-31:0":{"b": ["The vizier Ahmad b. Nizam al-Mulk was sent to Alamut with a large army; no result was achieved because of the winter", "ba5263e5"], "d": ["The Seljuk Sultan Muhammad Tapar dispatched his vizier Ahmad b. Nizam al-Mulk against Alamut with a large army in order to eliminate Hasan-i Sabbah; the campaign remained inconclusive because of the winter. The actual siege was to come in 1117.", "2e2a9c88"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:1113-06-18:0":{"b": ["Many Batinis were killed in Aleppo, together with Hasan-i Sabbah's deputies in Syria", "c70cc81f"], "d": ["The Seljuk Sultan Muhammad Tapar demanded that the Malik of Aleppo, Alp Arslan al-Akhras, and the ra'is al-ahdath, Sa'id b. Badi', have the Batinis in the city killed; many Batinis were killed, together with Hasan-i Sabbah's deputies in Syria such as Abu Tahir al-Sa'igh, Isma'il the da'i, and the brother of Hakim the astrologer (507/1113).", "c7adbffa"]},
